igh\":false,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"April 2025\",\"hasMultipleCatchmentAreas\":false},{\"servesHome\":true,\"greatSchoolsRating\":6,\"parentRating\":2,\"distanceInMiles\":\"0.9\",\"gradeRanges\":\"7-8\",\"institutionType\":\"Public\",\"name\":\"Sossaman Middle School\",\"schoolUrl\":\"\u002Fschool\u002F229048\u002FAZ\u002FQueen-Creek\u002FSossaman-Middle-School\",\"searchUrl\":\"\u002Fschool\u002F229048\u002FAZ\u002FQueen-Creek\u002FSossaman-Middle-School\",\"greatSchoolOverviewUrl\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fqueen-creek\u002F6786-Sossaman-Middle-School\u002F\",\"id\":229048,\"numberOfStudents\":1043,\"fullAddress\":\"18655 E Jacaranda Blvd, Queen Creek, AZ 85142\",\"numReviews\":6,\"studentToTeacherRatio\":19,\"websiteUrl\":\"http:\u002F\u002Fwww.husd.org\u002Fsossaman\",\"schoolReviews\":[{\"schoolId\":43362629,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"May 2025\",\"review\":\"This school has an impressive building and looks more like a small high school, but unfortunately, that’s where the positives end for us. If your child isn’t academically excelling or isn’t part of the majority racial group, don’t expect much support.My child was consistently bullied and fat-shamed throughout the year. Despite reporting these incidents, the administration did nothing—likely because my child had previously acted out in class. But acting out should be seen as a red flag that a student needs help, not a reason to ignore serious issues.Teachers made little effort to engage with or support students who weren’t already high performers. It felt like if your child didn’t fit into a narrow mold of success, they were written off.The overall experience was so discouraging that my child began dreading school. No family should have to go through that. If you’re looking for a supportive and inclusive environment, this might not be the right place.\",\"reviewerRating\":1,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":406786,\"maponicsId\":6961693,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fqueen-creek\u002F6786-Sossaman-Middle-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43362628,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"January 2025\",\"review\":\"The admin team is very responsive and visits classrooms daily to check in on staff and students. The office staff is friendly and helpful. Most teachers really seem to care about the kids and enjoy their jobs. The facility is very clean and well kept. Unfortunately, overall safety is a problem. Kids are caught daily vaping in the bathrooms and worse. Fights are recorded and shared rather than stopped. The SPED team needs to be overhauled. Some of the SPED teachers are downright rude and exclusive. There definitely needs to be more counselors per students on hand to properly deal with all of the daily drama.\",\"reviewerRating\":2,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":406786,\"maponicsId\":6768315,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fqueen-creek\u002F6786-Sossaman-Middle-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43362627,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"September 2024\",\"review\":\"I can’t say enough bad things about this school. Absolutely horrible experience. Teachers don’t care. My son had money stolen from him and the teacher told him, “I guess you learned a life lesson, now go have a seat”. Assistant principal does nothing. This school blames the kids while the staff provides no supervision or effort to even return emails. My son was struggling and wanted help. Couldn’t get anybody to help him. The epitome of what a disfunctional school looks like. Fights break out without anybody around to stop them. Completely out of control!\",\"reviewerRating\":1,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":406786,\"maponicsId\":6598512,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fqueen-creek\u002F6786-Sossaman-Middle-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43362626,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"April 2024\",\"review\":\"The IEP program here is a joke The schools teachers have no idea on how to handle kids with ADHD, autism etc They are very incompetent at meetings and im the classroom when situations arise and do not communicate with the students parents They will say your kids is doing something defiant but fail to acknowledge the IEP in place. They need more training as does the entire staff to restructure their system... They have had many complaints from parents from outside academies about IEP\\u0027s special education etc All I can say is be weary\",\"reviewerRating\":1,\"lastUpdatedDate\":\"June 2025\",\"institutionGreatschoolId\":406786,\"maponicsId\":6408884,\"url\":\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.greatschools.org\u002Farizona\u002Fqueen-creek\u002F6786-Sossaman-Middle-School\u002F\"},{\"schoolId\":43362625,\"reviewedBy\":\"Parent\",\"datePosted\":\"December 2019\",\"review\":\"DISCRIMINATION Students with cell phones have privileges to those without. When needing to send a message about a transportation emergency to my student during school I was told by front office to “text student”. When informing them she didn’t have a cell phone they continued that they could not interrupt class or pass a note on. Cooperation came after sending Mr. Dolan an email. Fast forward to now... I noticed my student left an assignment on the counter. Brought the assignment to school and ask that she pleased be called to get it. “Text student”they said. ”Student doesn’t have a phone” I reminded them. They continued that they couldn’t interrupt class for an assignment and that it’s a learning opportunity for student not to forget work. I said that it’s really unfair that a student with a cell phone can be interrupted in class, by their parents, to come get a forgotten assignment. While it’s a learning opportunity and no interruptions for the student without a cell phone. Basically the front desk encourages the parent to text a child and interrup